I sit at my desk in the office.
Eva comes over to me with a cup of coffee.
We are working closely together this week.
"Are you ready to look at the new layout?" she asks.
"Yes, I just need to open the program," I answer.
We look at the large screen together.
The big digital project finally looks good.
But suddenly I see a small error in the corner.
A blue button is a bit too far to the left.
"Look there, the position is wrong," I say.
Eva nods and points at the screen.
"You are right, we must move it to the right," she says.
I quickly write a few lines of code.
The button moves to the right place.
"Perfect, thank you for the help," Eva says and smiles warmly.
We talk relaxedly together about our plans for the weekend.
The work has become a safe and familiar routine now.
